{title: We Three Kings}
{artist: John Henry Hopkins Jr.}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 112}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]We three kings of [B7]Orient [Em]are
[Em]Bearing gifts we [B7]traverse a[Em]far
[Am]Field and fountain, [Em]moor and mountain
[B7]Following yonder [Em]star
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]star of won[D]der, star of [Em]night
[G]Star with royal [D]beauty [Em]bright
[Am]Westward leading, [Em]still proceeding
[B7]Guide us to Thy perfect [Em]light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Born a King on [B7]Bethlehem's [Em]plain
[Em]Gold I bring to [B7]crown Him a[Em]gain
[Am]King forever, [Em]ceasing never
[B7]Over us all to [Em]reign
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Frankincense to [B7]offer have [Em]I
[Em]Incense owns a [B7]Deity [Em]nigh
[Am]Prayer and praising, [Em]all men raising
[B7]Worship Him, God most [Em]high
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Em]Myrrh is mine, its [B7]bitter per[Em]fume
[Em]Breathes a life of [B7]gathering [Em]gloom
[Am]Sorrowing, sighing, [Em]bleeding, dying
[B7]Sealed in the stone-cold [Em]tomb
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Em]Glorious now be[B7]hold Him a[Em]rise
[Em]King and God and [B7]Sacri[Em]fice
[Am]Alleluia, [Em]Alleluia
[B7]Sounds through the earth and [Em]skies
{end_of_verse}
